WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.205
Lesson 1.3.

00:00:02.205 --> 00:00:04.985
Wallets, keys, hardware & multisig.

00:00:04.985 --> 00:00:06.849
By the end of this lesson, you'll

00:00:06.849 --> 00:00:08.329
be able to set up a wallet

00:00:08.329 --> 00:00:11.070
structure where one mistake can't lose everything.

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.660
Here's the plan.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.345
First, the key ideas.

00:00:15.345 --> 00:00:18.060
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.585
Then, your checklist.

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:21.747
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:23.047 --> 00:00:26.042
a website, never photograph it, never share it.

00:00:26.042 --> 00:00:28.972
No legitimate support team will ever ask for it.

00:00:28.972 --> 00:00:31.995
Compartmentalise: separate wallets by job, so a

00:00:31.995 --> 00:00:34.562
compromise only reaches one of them.

00:00:34.562 --> 00:00:37.477
First, Private key: the authority to sign.

00:00:37.477 --> 00:00:39.651
Whoever has it controls the funds.

00:00:39.651 --> 00:00:44.356
Next, Seed phrase: 12–24 words that recreate your keys.

00:00:44.356 --> 00:00:45.901
Never type it into.

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:49.631
Then, Hardware wallet: keeps keys on a separate device.

00:00:49.631 --> 00:00:52.196
Signing requires physical confirmation.

00:00:52.196 --> 00:00:54.823
Also, Multisig: needs M of N

00:00:54.823 --> 00:00:57.116
signers (e.g. 2 of 3).

00:00:57.116 --> 00:00:59.231
Good for large or shared funds.

00:00:59.231 --> 00:01:02.309
And finally, Smart wallets: contract accounts that

00:01:02.309 --> 00:01:05.146
can add spending limits, recovery and batching.

00:01:06.446 --> 00:01:09.333
Move money down the chain (vault → operator →

00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:12.771
burner) only as needed, and sweep profits back up.

00:01:12.771 --> 00:01:14.548
If the burner gets drained, you

00:01:14.548 --> 00:01:16.570
lose only the burner's balance.

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:19.395
Vault, Long-term holdings, Almost never.

00:01:19.395 --> 00:01:22.555
No DeFi approvals, Hardware (or multisig).

00:01:22.555 --> 00:01:28.245
Operator, Active DeFi positions, Known, verified protocols only, Hardware.

00:01:28.245 --> 00:01:30.546
Burner, Small amounts for new apps,

00:01:30.546 --> 00:01:33.805
mints, airdrops, Anything experimental, Hot wallet.

00:01:35.105 --> 00:01:38.120
Let's look at the diagram: The 3-wallet setup.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:39.680
Take a moment with it.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.090
It's everything we've just said, in one picture.

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:44.850
Here's your checklist.

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.385
Do it now, for real.

00:01:46.385 --> 00:01:48.634
First, Seed phrase stored offline,

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:50.990
in two separate physical places.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:54.752
Next, Vault wallet has never approved a DeFi contract.

00:01:54.752 --> 00:01:57.537
Then, Separate burner wallet for anything new.

00:01:57.537 --> 00:02:00.160
And finally, I read every signing prompt on

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:03.082
the hardware device screen, not just the website.

00:02:04.382 --> 00:02:05.592
Question 1.

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:08.011
A "support agent" in DMs needs your

00:02:08.011 --> 00:02:10.932
seed phrase to fix a stuck transaction.

00:02:10.932 --> 00:02:11.782
What do you do?

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.937
The answer: Nothing.

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:19.842
It's a scam, every time.

00:02:19.842 --> 00:02:21.042
Block and report.

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:23.587
Question 2.

00:02:23.587 --> 00:02:25.802
Why keep the vault wallet free of approvals?

00:02:30.222 --> 00:02:33.762
The answer: Approvals let contracts move your tokens.

00:02:33.762 --> 00:02:36.606
With none, a compromised protocol can't reach it.

00:02:37.906 --> 00:02:39.176
Question 3.

00:02:39.176 --> 00:02:41.711
What does 2-of-3 multisig protect against?

00:02:46.131 --> 00:02:49.321
The answer: A single lost or compromised key.

00:02:49.321 --> 00:02:51.631
Two signers are still needed to move funds.

00:02:52.931 --> 00:02:54.176
Let's recap.

00:02:54.176 --> 00:02:56.681
Private key: the authority to sign.

00:02:56.681 --> 00:03:00.786
Seed phrase: 12–24 words that recreate your keys.

00:03:00.786 --> 00:03:04.161
Hardware wallet: keeps keys on a separate device.

00:03:04.161 --> 00:03:06.203
Multisig: needs M of N

00:03:06.203 --> 00:03:08.156
signers (e.g. 2 of 3).

00:03:09.456 --> 00:03:11.971
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:11.971 --> 00:03:16.393
Next up, Lesson 1.4: Tokens, approvals & allowances.
